 like  gasoline or food at home or exploding  upwards and why is it that our  politicians rather than actually taking  action to go ahead and get these prices  down or simply tweeting at companies  telling them to stop price gouging when  we can easily see that these independent  sometimes family-owned gas stations  they're simply trying to make a living  like everyone else  these situations are complex the global  macro environment is impossible to  predict but what we do know is that we  need less complaining and we need more  competing we need free markets and we  need free market solutions to these  problems because right now what we have  is a manipulated Market where central  banks and politicians around the world  continue to intervene  the free market can't work if their  hands are tied behind its back  instead allow the free market to get to  work get the intervention out of the way  and something tells me that we'll get  the corrections the reversions to the  mean that we so desperately seem to need
 

